    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this bright and spacious two-bedroom apartment to the market in the ever-popular Jervis Place development, ideally located on Abbey Street in the heart of Dublin City Centre. No. 107 is presented in good condition throughout and offers an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, investors, or those seeking a conveniently located city residence within walking distance of every conceivable amenity.\r\n\r\nThe location is truly second to none. Situated in the heart of Dublin 1, Jervis Place enjoys immediate access to an abundance of cafés, restaurants, shops, bars, and cultural attractions. The Jervis Shopping Centre, Henry Street, O'Connell Street, Temple Bar, Trinity College, the IFSC, and the Four Courts are all within a short stroll. The LUAS Red Line stops just moments from the development, while Dublin Bus routes, Connolly Station, Tara Street Station, and Heuston Station are all easily accessible, making commuting around the city and beyond effortless.\r\n\r\nBright and well-laid-out internal living accommodation extending to c.47 sq.m. comprises an entrance hallway, a spacious open plan living/dining room with access to the kitchen, two well-proportioned bedrooms, and a fully tiled family bathroom. The apartment also benefits from access to well-maintained communal courtyard, providing a peaceful outdoor space in the heart of the city.\r\n\r\nNo. 107 comes to the market vacant and chain free, allowing for a straightforward purchase. Additional benefits include lift access, double glazed windows, electric heating, and a highly sought-after city centre location. This is an ideal opportunity for purchasers looking to step onto the property ladder or investors seeking a property in one of Dublin's most convenient and established locations.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is highly advised. Contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today on 086 8323302 or 01 541 1455 to arrange a viewing.\r\n\r\nKey Features\r\n•BER C \r\n•c.47 sq.m \r\n•Built in 1995 \r\n•Vacant & chain free \r\n•Bright and spacious living accommodation \r\n•Double glazed windows \r\n•Electric heating \r\n•Lift access \r\n•Overlooking communal gardens \r\n•Access to well-maintained communal courtyard\r\n•Well-maintained development \r\n•Excellent city centre location \r\n•LUAS Red Line within a short walk \r\n•Walking distance to Jervis Shopping Centre, Henry Street, Temple Bar & Trinity College \r\n•Ideal for first-time buyers and investors \r\n•Early viewing highly advised"
      },
      {
